# Run mutex — process-local, never committed
.run.lock/

# Verbose per-run logs: results are durable, logs are not.
#
# Both patterns are needed. `runs/*/*/logs/` is where run.sh tees, but a log
# launched by hand lands at runs/<provider>/<name>.log, one level higher — ten
# of those were committed before this rule covered them. They carry no
# credentials, but they do carry operational detail (subscription reset times,
# proxy errors) that has no business in a public repository.
runs/*/*/logs/
runs/**/*.log
